<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>A Step-by-Step Guide to Implementing Inventory Management</b></h3>
                <p>An inventory management solution can help manufacturers track stock, materials, movements, replenishment, and warehouse activities through centralized digital workflows.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Inventory Strategy Planning: Identify stock, warehouse, material, replenishment, movement, and reporting requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Centralized Inventory Data: Maintain structured information for products, materials, stock levels, locations, and inventory transactions.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Inventory Workflow Automation: Automate stock updates, replenishment alerts, approvals, notifications, and routine inventory activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Secure Access: Apply role-based access controls to protect inventory and business information.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Continuous Inventory Optimization: Use inventory analytics, feedback, and operational data to improve stock management.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>Key Critical Factors for a Successful Inventory Management Solution</b></h3>
                <p>Inventory management requires accurate data, real-time visibility, replenishment controls, integration, security, and user-friendly workflows.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Clear Inventory Objectives: Define measurable goals for inventory accuracy, availability, turnover, replenishment, and carrying costs.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Accurate Stock Data: Maintain current item, location, quantity, movement, and transaction information.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Replenishment Automation: Automate reorder alerts, approvals, stock notifications, and routine inventory tasks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  System Integration: Connect inventory with production, procurement, sales, warehouse, and ERP systems.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  User Adoption: Provide simple inventory workflows and training for warehouse and operations teams.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Inventory Management" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Inventory Management" /></div>
            </div>
