<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 me-3 p-3" alt="Inventory Management" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Inventory Management" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Inventory Management Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>
                <p>Manufacturers may struggle with stock inaccuracies, overstocking, shortages, manual tracking, and disconnected warehouse processes.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Inaccurate Stock Levels: Use centralized inventory records and structured transaction workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Stock Shortages: Configure replenishment alerts and inventory visibility to support timely action.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Excess Inventory: Use inventory analytics and demand information to improve stock planning.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Manual Tracking: Automate inventory transactions, notifications, and routine warehouse activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Disconnected Warehouse Data: Integrate inventory with production, procurement, sales, and ERP systems.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>The Importance of Customization in Inventory Management</b></h3>
                <p>Manufacturers have different warehouses, stock structures, materials, replenishment rules, and movement processes. Customization helps inventory workflows match operational requirements.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Customize Inventory Workflows: Align receiving, issuing, transfers, adjustments, and replenishment with business processes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Create Role-Based Workspaces: Provide warehouse, procurement, production, and management teams with relevant actions.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Automate Replenishment: Configure alerts and workflows around stock thresholds and material requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Build Inventory Dashboards: Provide insights into stock levels, turnover, shortages, excess, and warehouse performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Gather User Feedback: Continuously improve inventory workflows based on operational results.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

