<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Managing Change for Successful Inventory Management Adoption</b></h3>
                <p>Inventory accuracy depends on consistent user behavior and disciplined digital processes. Change management helps teams adopt the new workflows.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Explain the Inventory Vision: Communicate how better inventory visibility improves production and operational efficiency.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Engage Warehouse Teams: Involve warehouse, procurement, production, finance, and management users.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Role-Based Training: Train users on inventory transactions and workflows relevant to their roles.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Roll Out in Phases: Introduce inventory functions progressively and monitor data quality.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Ongoing Support: Address process questions and continuously improve inventory operations.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>How to Optimize Inventory Management for Maximum ROI</b></h3>
                <p>Inventory management should continuously evolve to balance availability, accuracy, working capital, and operational efficiency.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Define Inventory KPIs: Measure accuracy, turnover, stockouts, excess inventory, carrying levels, and fulfillment performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Integrate Core Systems: Connect inventory with production, procurement, sales, warehouse, and ERP applications.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Improve User Experience: Simplify stock transactions, searches, approvals, and warehouse workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Review Inventory Performance: Regularly assess stock levels, movements, accuracy, and operational outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Leverage Automation and Analytics: Use alerts, dashboards, and analytics to improve inventory decisions.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Inventory Management" /></div>
